With 370 PFS events at IA1, the study has \(\sim 72 \%\) power for detecting a PFS HR of 0.7 at 0.0095 (one-sided) and \(\sim 84 \%\) power for detecting a HR of 0.7 at 0.025 (one-sided). With 468 PFS events at IA2, the study has \(\sim 90 \%\) power for detecting a HR of 0.7 at 0.0095 (one-sided) and \(\sim 96 \%\) power for detecting a HR of 0.7 at 0.025 (one-sided). The duration of PFS in the control group is assumed to follow an exponential distribution with a median of 6.5 months based on historical data. The assumed follow-up time after last patient enrolled is 13 months for IA2. An exponential dropout rate of \(0.35 \%\) per month is assumed. \\
